WEBVTT

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:28.790
Pearson...

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.390
Time passes fast.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.820
It's already been three years.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:43.430
What's going on?

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:51.160
Pearson!

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.690
Just wait, I'll rescue you!

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:56.820
Crow.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:00.440
Pearson, what happened?

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:04.460
This doesn't concern you.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.970
This is a personal issue.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:10.410
But more importantly, take my Blackbird!

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:11.880
Blackbird?

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:16.920
Take care of the kids.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.210
Pearson!

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.370
Bolger...

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:55.420
Huh?

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.320
Bruno fiddled with something again.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:03.220
I don't know if he's improving 
or breaking my machine.

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:07.840
It started.

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:11.060
See you, Pearson.  I'll come again.

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:38.300
Every time you're hurt, you can become kinder

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:43.840
Stand up and you'll understand strength

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:48.420
Don't look back and keep going

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:54.080
Both the past and the future 
are connected to the present

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:59.120
There's no need to fear

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:06.760
I'll keep telling you that you're not alone

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:12.900
The passionate emotions in your heart

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:18.540
Streak to the infinite future

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:24.130
Dreams surpass their limits

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:32.050
And will lead you to a bright place

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:03.910
Reminiscence  Friend's Entrusted Legacy

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:12.820
Strange.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:18.190
Why does the engage stimulator stop 
working when I put in the decroncer?

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:24.550
What's this circuit?

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:30.650
What is it?

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:33.640
There's a strange circuit.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:34.890
Strange circuit?

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:37.510
It has something to do with this part.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:39.700
What's this?

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:43.190
You guys!

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:46.330
What are you doing this time?

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:47.600
Hey, Crow.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:52.080
When I was adjusting the program, 
I found a strange circuit.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.300
Strange circuit?

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:57.530
No matter what I do, I can't 
access it any further.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:01.980
Don't fiddle with it too 
much and break my machine.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:05.120
I can't work without Blackbird.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:06.070
Don't worry, Crow.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:07.710
We won't do anything crazy.

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:09.720
Let's investigate a little more.

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:11.580
Let's mute and insert the deck.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:13.920
We'll have to first free the potential.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:15.880
Excuse me.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:18.250
Ushio and Mikage.

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:20.720
Do you have a second, Crow?

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:28.270
What is it?

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:31.530
It's about Robert Pearson.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.270
How do you know Pearson?

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:36.590
You think that I don't know him?

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:39.400
Satellite used to be my jurisdiction.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.280
But why now?

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:44.140
We want to ask you something 
about Pearson's death.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:45.630
Ask me something?

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:46.110
Yes.

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:51.420
We found out that Pearson was dueling 
someone before the incident.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:53.590
The opponent used this card.

00:05:57.570 --> 00:06:00.240
We're looking for the person who used it.

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:01.130
Do you know?

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:05.950
Crimson Mefist...  I 
never heard of this card.

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:07.750
I see.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:15.460
A long time ago, they were developing new 
cards whose effects were more than just visuals.

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:21.880
They made dangerous cards that 
actually dealt damage to the player.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:23.620
Dealt actual damage?

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:27.580
They immediately stopped development.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:32.090
But several prototype cards 
were released into the world.

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:34.830
That's one of them.

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:40.220
So Pearson took damage from 
this card's effect and lost.

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:58.570
Luckily, only a few cards were leaked.

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:03.800
If we find the owner of that card, 
we'll know who killed Pearson.

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:07.320
We thought that you might know something.

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:10.260
Crimson Mefist...

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:19.490
What a blissful scent.

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:22.710
Jack, today is...

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:27.160
I'm borrowing this, Jack!

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:31.370
My Wheel of Fortune!

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:33.710
What are you thinking, Crow?

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:34.760
Umm...

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:35.710
What is it?

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:36.920
I'm sorry!

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:47.830
Bolger knew Pearson for a long time, 
so he might know about that card.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:51.520
WRGP World Riding Grand Prix!

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:54.000
Boil up, battle spirit!  Burn up, soul!

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.070
D-Wheelers, gather here!

00:07:56.720 --> 00:08:00.810
Bolger & Company support the WRGP.

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:06.280
Bolger & Company's PXV3A is capable 
of making high speed turns!

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:11.680
Experience new Riding Duels with the PXV3A!

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:28.750
Well well...

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:31.910
Do you like it?  It's a first printing 
of Witch of the Black Forest.

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:36.060
No wonder you're the president 
of Bolger & Company.

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:38.960
They're all wonderful cards.

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:40.480
So do I get the loan?

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:42.150
Loan?

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:44.950
You must be kidding.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:53.830
They're wonderful cards, but they're not good 
enough collateral to let you borrow so much money.

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:59.430
I would reconsider if you have the 
legendary Black-Winged Dragon card.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:04.310
Black-Winged Dragon...

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:15.610
Let me go!

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:20.450
C'mon!  I have business with Bolger!

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:24.460
If you want to meet the 
president, make an appointment.

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:26.430
That's not necessary for him.

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:30.130
He's my friend.

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:31.600
Bolger!

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:34.180
It's been a long time, Crow!

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:37.940
I apologize for their behavior.

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:40.110
Want something to drink?

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:42.510
No, I'm fine.

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:46.780
I heard stories, but I now 
see how successful you are.

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:49.580
You're the world's top D-Wheel maker.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:50.720
You're on a totally different level.

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:55.860
We finally completed the test 
course for new D-Wheel models.

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:59.690
The young people in the factory work hard.

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:01.660
They're reliable.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:04.430
Anyway, it's been a long time.

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:05.400
Yeah.

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:07.210
It's been three years.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.730
Three years?

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:11.870
I see.  We haven't met since that day.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.280
I can't believe that happened.

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:24.200
About that, we might be able 
to find out who killed Pearson.

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:27.020
What?  Find out who killed Pearson?

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:27.620
Yeah.

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:32.030
Before Pearson was killed, 
he dueled against someone.

00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:35.400
We now know the opponent's card.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:38.410
I thought you might know something, Bolger.

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:42.620
You know something!

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:46.270
Tell me!  Who killed Pearson?

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:47.960
Bolger!

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:51.610
Forget about it, Crow.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:55.720
What's the point of searching 
for the criminal now?

00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:58.580
That won't make Pearson happy.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:03.450
Anyway, how about working in my factory?

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:06.820
Are you serious?

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:12.840
I can't believe you would tell 
me to forget about Pearson!

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:14.800
I see.

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:20.040
Now that you're a big-time president, you 
don't have time to deal with the past!

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:23.580
It was foolish of me to ask for your help!

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:24.860
Sorry to bother you!

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:28.740
Crow!

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:36.880
If you want to know so badly, I'll tell you.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.450
But only if you defeat me in a duel!

00:11:39.770 --> 00:11:40.700
A duel?

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:44.190
That's right.  If you can 
defeat me, I'll tell you.

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:50.430
But if I win, I get your Black-Winged Dragon.

00:11:50.780 --> 00:11:52.590
Black-Winged Dragon?

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:55.040
You mean Pearson's card?

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:57.070
Synchro Summon!

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:59.240
Black-Winged Dragon!

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:02.980
But that card was lost in the fire.

00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:05.240
You don't have to keep it a secret.

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:11.040
Before Pearson died, I know that he 
entrusted you with Blackbird and Black-Winged Dragon.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:12.320
What are you talking about?

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:13.950
I don't know anything about that card.

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:17.360
Let me speak candidly.

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:19.930
I'm in trouble due to lack of money.

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:22.970
At this rate, I'll have to close the factory.

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:28.170
But if I have Black-Winged Dragon, I 
can use it as collateral to get a loan!

00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:29.040
Collateral?

00:12:29.530 --> 00:12:31.710
I know what you're going to say.

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:35.820
You won't allow Pearson's card 
to be used as collateral.

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:39.880
But let me say one thing.

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:43.850
If Pearson was in my position, 
he would do the same.

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:45.690
Pearson?

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:53.760
Think carefully whether this 
was something Pearson would do.

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:59.130
If you want to know, then 
challenge me to a duel!

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:01.900
The location will be my 
company's test course!

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:28.490
Crow...

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:31.100
Pearson?

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:35.480
Yeah.  He left Blackbird 
to me before he died.

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:36.470
I owe him everything.

00:13:37.490 --> 00:13:41.340
It was soon after Kiryu was captured.

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:46.940
Without any goals, I lived aimlessly.

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:49.400
Then one day...

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:57.250
Dad?

00:13:57.750 --> 00:13:58.720
Dad!

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:04.060
As usual, Satellite's factory used him up.

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:06.520
Here's your money.

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:09.980
But we deducted the transportation fee.

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:12.370
How dare you!

00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:15.000
Take that!

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:17.220
Crow!

00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:21.920
Don't get uppity, you Satellite punk!

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:23.100
Let's go.

00:14:32.020 --> 00:14:34.040
Who's that?

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:39.760
You want to fight us?

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:42.200
Interesting.  Let's duel!

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:45.860
Hail the Iron Hammer attacks you directly!

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:51.010
I activate the trap Shadow Dance!

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:01.400
Wow!

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:06.090
I Synchro Summon Black-Winged Dragon!

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:14.860
Damn!

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:16.860
You'll regret this!

00:15:20.840 --> 00:15:23.320
That's how I met Pearson.

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:29.340
Pearson gathered and took care of 
Satellite children, just like me.

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:34.510
He taught them job skills so that 
they can be self-independent.

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:37.320
I thought this was great.

00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:41.180
Pearson and I decided to work together.

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:45.430
Pearson gave me hope to live again.

00:15:45.890 --> 00:15:50.200
With the first-ever engine created in 
Satellite, we would surprise the citizens of the City.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:53.530
Pearson's D-Wheel development excited me.

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:56.180
But one day...

00:15:59.610 --> 00:16:01.380
What's going on?

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:04.180
Pearson!

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:06.840
Just wait, I'll rescue you!

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:10.420
Crow.

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:14.300
Take care of the kids.

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:18.410
Pearson!

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:28.000
After I lost Pearson, I 
didn't know what to do.

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:33.050
All I could do was steal 
cards to make the kids happy.

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:38.060
Bolger is great.

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:43.530
He took over Pearson's legacy and built a 
D-Wheel factory in the former Satellite.

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:50.880
All I'm doing is atoning for my past actions.

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:53.560
Because I failed to take 
over Pearson's legacy.

00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:56.970
That's not true.

00:16:56.970 --> 00:16:59.670
You're continuing Pearson's 
legacy wonderfully.

00:17:00.530 --> 00:17:02.040
Me?

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.670
Crow!

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:06.400
What are you doing?

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:08.810
Crow, hurry up and come over here!

00:17:08.810 --> 00:17:10.070
Crow!

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:12.670
Look at the smiles on their faces.

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:16.970
You're the one who gave them smiles of hope.

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:20.400
There's no need to feel ashamed.

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:23.750
You should travel the 
path that you believe in.

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:26.570
Yusei...

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:30.190
What?  A battle?

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:38.040
But that guy didn't give 
Black-Winged Dragon to Crow.

00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:39.350
Yeah.

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:42.400
But this is Crow's response.

00:17:45.950 --> 00:17:48.480
All right.  I'll go with him.

00:18:04.340 --> 00:18:05.690
You're fine with this?

00:18:06.220 --> 00:18:07.360
Of course.

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:09.930
I'll continue Pearson's legacy in my own way.

00:18:10.510 --> 00:18:13.050
Fine.  Let's battle, Crow!

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:17.770
Speed World 2 set!

00:18:20.270 --> 00:18:21.690
Riding Duel!

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:24.410
Acceleration!

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:35.690
What unbelievable acceleration!

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:38.660
That's why it's the newest D-Wheel model.

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:54.340
I took the first corner, so I'll go first.

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:55.810
My turn!

00:18:56.140 --> 00:19:00.200
I summon White Warrior - Fog the 
Treasure Shield in defense position.

00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:04.220
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:19:04.730 --> 00:19:06.560
2000 defense points...

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:07.770
My turn!

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:14.660
When monsters are only on your field, I can 
summon this card without releasing another monster!

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:18.250
I summon Blackwing - Sirocco the Dawn!

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:26.410
I can Special Summon this card 
when a Blackwing is on my field!

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:29.970
Appear, Blackwing - Bora the Spear!

00:19:32.860 --> 00:19:38.250
Due to Sirocco the Dawn's effect, I can 
concentrate the Blackwings' power on Bora the Spear!

00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:44.460
Good!  It has more than the 
opponent's 2000 defense points!

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:47.130
Not good enough, Crow.

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:49.460
I activate the Continuous Trap Whiteout!

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:58.500
Whiteout negates all effects that 
your monsters give to other monsters!

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:07.230
Each individual monster isn't dangerous, but 
they create power by calling for their teammates.

00:20:07.230 --> 00:20:09.910
That bond is the Blackwing 
deck's special feature.

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:12.650
So I will sever that bond!

00:20:13.760 --> 00:20:15.930
Now your Blackwings are isolated.

00:20:15.930 --> 00:20:23.090
As long as Whiteout is active, Blackwings 
can't rely on their teammates nor give them power!

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:25.560
This is bad for Crow!

00:20:26.770 --> 00:20:27.760
I end my turn.

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:29.460
My turn.

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:34.040
I summon White Warrior 
- Hail the Iron Hammer.

00:20:34.970 --> 00:20:38.440
Then I activate the Continuous 
Trap Sacred Arrow!

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:41.150
At the End Phase,

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:44.240
each player takes 400 points of 
damage for every one of his monsters

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:46.180
that was destroyed that turn.

00:20:47.240 --> 00:20:50.150
400 points for every destroyed monster?

00:20:50.510 --> 00:20:53.120
Hail the Iron Hammer attacks Bora the Spear!

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:55.220
Hammer Attack!

00:20:58.930 --> 00:21:03.230
When Hail the Iron Hammer 
destroys your monster in battle,

00:21:03.230 --> 00:21:06.230
another monster on your field is destroyed!

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:12.010
At the end of the turn, you 
take Sacred Arrow's effect.

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:21.850
Crow!

00:21:22.530 --> 00:21:25.000
He uses Whiteout to sever the monsters' bond,

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:27.300
and he uses Sacred Arrow to deal damage.

00:21:28.150 --> 00:21:30.830
This is an anti-Blackwing deck!

00:21:34.800 --> 00:21:38.270
Bring it, Crow!  It's your turn!

00:22:08.030 --> 00:22:13.020
The small cliff floats on the Milky Way

00:22:13.020 --> 00:22:17.900
The sights I see are different 
than what I imagined

00:22:17.900 --> 00:22:22.840
Were you able to move on from the past?

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:27.850
The answer isn't no, but 
there's something missing

00:22:27.850 --> 00:22:32.900
The cruel god tests us

00:22:32.900 --> 00:22:39.460
Let's fill the emptiness 
and head to the next stage

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:43.530
If you ask me "What's our relationship?"

00:22:43.530 --> 00:22:49.370
We're more than friends... 
but that's not quite right

00:22:49.370 --> 00:22:53.460
Bond is the proper word

00:22:53.460 --> 00:22:59.080
As we fight, we understand each other

00:22:59.080 --> 00:23:02.260
"Where are you right now?"  "On Earth"

00:23:02.260 --> 00:23:04.520
Because I'm not an astronaut

00:23:04.520 --> 00:23:09.050
I have no problems when 
I'm below the ozone layer

00:23:09.050 --> 00:23:12.020
"I know, I'm coming right away."

00:23:12.020 --> 00:23:15.460
You want to party until the morning

00:23:15.460 --> 00:23:18.840
At our special place
